# aws-session registry. One line per alias; lines starting with # are ignored.
# Copy to ~/.config/aws-session/sessions.conf and chmod 600.
#
# alias        The profile name in ~/.aws/config, and the name passed to aws-session.
# account_id   The account this alias must resolve to. Any other account is an error.
# region       Written into the env file as AWS_REGION and AWS_DEFAULT_REGION.
# sso_session  The [sso-session <name>] block in ~/.aws/config. Leave it empty for a
#              paste-only alias (break-glass credentials, no SSO).
# description  Free text shown by `aws-session list`.
#
# alias      | account_id   | region    | sso_session | description
staging      | 111111111111 | us-east-1 | example     | Staging, AdministratorAccess
prod-read    | 222222222222 | us-east-1 | example     | Production, ReadOnlyAccess
vendor       | 333333333333 | eu-west-1 |             | Third-party account, pasted credentials only
